WEBVTT
NOTE OpenIE Research TV — spellcheck (90s) AI-synthesized studio narration

1
00:00:02.501 --> 00:00:05.492
Nobody budgets tokens before fixing a typo today,

2
00:00:05.492 --> 00:00:09.705
yet early spell checkers were marketed as elite productivity engines.

3
00:00:16.356 --> 00:00:19.648
Dated catalogs from CP/M and DOS through modern mobile

4
00:00:19.648 --> 00:00:24.098
OSes trace an exact economic transition driven by algorithmic efficiency.

5
00:00:30.750 --> 00:00:34.597
This three-dimensional globe contrasts centralized high-watt server hubs

6
00:00:34.597 --> 00:00:38.177
with lightweight skills running locally across billions of devices.

7
00:00:44.828 --> 00:00:47.921
Inline tools succeed when latency is imperceptible,

8
00:00:47.921 --> 00:00:51.681
false positives are bounded, and battery drain goes unnoticed.

9
00:00:58.333 --> 00:01:03.179
Today's frontier AI resembles standalone 1982 software: impressive,

10
00:01:03.179 --> 00:01:06.578
power-hungry, and priced per seat or per token.

11
00:01:13.230 --> 00:01:20.449
Compiling verified capabilities into sub-millijoule local tables repeats the spell-check trajectory for computer intelligence.
